Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||12-11-2001||04:36 PM||||that should only apply to cars in poor running condition, right?<P>there was a program started in Canada where obviously unsafe vehicles are being pulled over for roadside inspections, and the plates are taken away if the vehicle does not pass. I think that's great.. I've seen many old rusted out jacked up pickup trucks, with either no exhaust or some crappy system with a cherrybomb in it.. driven by stupid hicks, who drive on the wrong side of the road for half a mile when making a left turn.... usually have their hats adjusted too small, and just sitting on the front of their heads.<P>or people who drive old 80s cars with the bumpers hanging off, muffler dragging on the ground.. no seatbelts.. ashtrays crammed full and cigarette butts on the floormats cause they're too lazy to empty the ashtrays.. garbage in the back seat..<P>in case you're wondering, there are specific people that match these descriptions that I'm referring to.. but I do hate those things in general.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Some old cars are nice, and people want to restore them.. others are just ugly old beaters, and I'm sure we can find much better uses for the steel and glass that the cars are made of.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000007||JohnF||12-11-2001||04:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B><BR>...there was a program started in Canada where obviously unsafe vehicles are being pulled over for roadside inspections others are just ugly old beaters...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In that case, I'm glad I live where I live.  I would hate to think that some entity was empowered by a Federal government to make a <B>judgement</B> about MY personal property as to whether it met THEIR criteria for usefulness or "ugly" even.  <P>First, the Federal government empowers that ability as regard cars, then down the slippery slope we go.  Whatever some politician believes is offensive to them and their constituency should be (and would be) banned under that criteria.<P>I don't care how many garbage cans full is in another's back seat or front seat or anywhere else as long as the operator doesn't infringe on my ability to also use that road.  <P>If it does, it is the operator's fault, not the garbage!<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||10
Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||12-11-2001||05:38 PM||||I think that the worst of this bill is twofold:<P>First, cars "purchased" by us (our tax dollars) are not allowed to go to salvage, i.e. someone can strip a perfectly good or rebuildable alternator, brake caliper, steering rack, or an entire engine/ transmission. The problem here is that a) hot rodders (like us) miss out on a great collection of parts for our hobby, and b) the industry that lives on such activity, for those of us who don't want to build our own engine, or just need a recon part, gets stripped heavily, putting people out of work and out of business.<P>Second, let's say you're a person living below the median, living in an apartment near the city, and you rely on your car to get around. The government sends you a letter saying, "Hey, we noticed based on your registration that you've got a 1970 Pontiac LeMans in your driveway. How about we give you $500 to scrap it, and a voucher for $1500 towards a 2002 car? Just drive it to XXX Scrapyard and fill out these papers!" Well, that's $2000! As stated above, the LeMans's small block is lost forever, and you take your $1500 voucher (You spent the $500 on a new 31" TV because you were so smart) to the dealer, only to find out that your car payments are $390, and your insurance will triple....<P>You (not us. Editorial "you.") might even buy a Honda....||||reg||1
Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||12-11-2001||08:55 PM||||the "ugly beater" comment was made by <B>me...</B> not the government. the canadian gov was going after cars with rusty frames, non-functional brakes, broken windshields, broken lights, etc.... safety stuff.. I know that if there was a car that wouldn't pass safety for something like a rusty frame (like my 84.. now parked forever...) flying down the highway towards me at 80mph... if it breaks, there's a chance people could get hurt. I think that's a much bigger concern than what the fuel economy is.<P>the ones on the news looked like they should have been in a scrapyard, but they were on the 401... a MAJOR highway (avg. speed during rushour is 80mph or higher)<P>all they were doing was pulling unsafe vehicles off the roads, no mention of any age, appearance, etc.. I said the stuff about the ugly beater cars, cause I hate them.. I see so many 1980s tempos with multi colored panels, and 1970s cars done in primer and rust... it's horrible, is it really so hard for people to get a can of spray paint from walmart and just do a couple of coats of paint??? it's not perfect, but better than what it is now..<P>there are some cars that people are NEVER gonna restore on a large scale, so when one breaks down.. strip it, and scrap it.. so our fieros might have a new V8, or some new wheels, etc...<P>besides, if they want to enhance the mileage of america's cars... DO SOMETHING ABOUT ALL THE IDIOTS WHO DRIVE BIG SUVS JUST BECAUSE THEY'RE POPULAR!!<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000010||Silver88GT||12-11-2001||10:53 PM||||Sorry to get political.  Was trying to avoid doing it on PFF (especially since I don't think there are any PFF members in my voting district  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">),  but I can't help myself on this one.  If you want to truly solve the problem of ridiculous government regulations that infringe on our freedoms, lead to more problems than they solve, and waste tax payer dollars....Vote Libertarian!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||12-11-2001||11:10 PM||||Silver: I have a good friend who's libertarian, we've had many discussions about politics.. he's quite a radical, one of his ideas was to move all of humanity off the earth onto space stations, and strip mine the earth, except small pockets of areas for parks, for recreation..<P>I think the idea of socialized medicine is ok, cause I can go to a hospital and get whatever treatment I need, and not notice ANY changes in the taxes I pay.. but people abuse the system like crazy. welfare is even worse.. I say bring back the foodstamps.. probably in some sort of debit card form though. welfare money shouldn't be used to buy booze and smokes.. especially if a child is going hungry because there's no money left for proper food. the canadian gov wastes all our tax money.<P>(I really enjoyed my political science elective class last semester..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>I think libertarianism has many benefits, all the exposure I've had to it has been fairly extremist though. I'd love to discuss some of the pros/cons of it, email me!<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000012||Silver88GT||12-12-2001||01:11 PM||||Wow, sounds like your buddy is radical!<P>There are a lot of people that call themselves libertarian (with a little l) whose views are quite far removed from the Libertarian Party (big L).  We are simply for smaller government, lower taxes, and more personal freedom.  Basically do what you want with yourself and your money as long as you don't harm someone else's self or money.  <P>It is not radical at all, it is what our Founding Fathers had in mind when they formed this great nation.  You do have to be careful though, because there is a lot of rhetoric out there that sounds Libertarian that really is not.  <P>OK, that's enough politics for PFF. :-) Glad that you're interested in learning more.  I'll e-mail you.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Hartz||12-12-2001||01:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>the "ugly beater" comment was made by [b]me...</B> <P>...I said the stuff about the ugly beater cars, cause I hate them.. I see so many 1980s tempos with multi colored panels, and 1970s cars done in primer and rust... it's horrible, is it really so hard for people to get a can of spray paint from walmart and just do a couple of coats of paint??? it's not perfect, but better than what it is now..<P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh oh.  My car is an 80's car.  And my car has ugly, multi-colored panels.  And my friends think having a V8 in a little car is unsafe...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>Gonna have to have the dog start sleeping in the garage to protect my toys...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Patrick's Dad||12-12-2001||02:14 PM||||I don't have a problem with old rusted out Dodge Aspens and Ford Econolines being taken off the road and put into a boneyard where no one can drive them, but usable parts can be removed and reconditioned. I do have a problem with the government sending me a letter enticing me with someone else's money (A small part of it mine), encouraging me to scrap my 1974 Valiant forever. I'm planning to drop a 360 into it with a 727OD (which would have to come from a Dodge truck, which would be sitting in a boneyard), among other things. Plus, in a year or so, I'd be getting a letter about my Formula. Imagine the tax money they're spending on postage alone.<P>Everything the government has done, save for defending our shores, has been a colossal failure. Back off everything but the original Bill of Rights, which is what the forefathers intended. Realize that taking my money for anything but funding the Armed Services, building infrastructure (roads and bridges), and precious little else is a waste of money, mine and yours.<P>Socialized medicine? Well, we've done so well with welfare that I'm sure we could manage our country right into bankruptcy. The only ones whose hands belong in my pockets are me and my woman, the latter to signal extracurricular activity.||||reg||1
Z||000015||GTFiero1||12-12-2001||09:46 PM||||Honda Insite! those things are butt-ugly.  15years old or more. most cars are front wheel drive now. a man cant live on front drive alone!<P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_3.jpg">   <BR>you gotta keep on keepin on...<BR>IM AOL: GTFiero &  Rumpdetective (dont ask)||||reg||1
Z||000016||fieroX||12-13-2001||01:17 AM||||Come on and get them.  I have both a 87 fiero and a 73 firebird formula.  If they want to crush either of my cars they will have to pry the keys from my cold dead hands.  But before that happens they will be introduced to my 300 win mag.  It does a lovely job on a deer.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif">  </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroX.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroX.com</A><BR>coming soon L67 powered 87 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000017||Blacktree||12-13-2001||02:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>But before that happens they will be introduced to my 300 win mag. It does a lovely job on a deer.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>That is, if they (the gov't) haven't taken your win mag away by then...<P>Politicians have always tried to tackle problems the most difficult and least efficient way possible. <P>Look at how they decided to fight crime. They think if they make weapons illegal, the crime rates will drop. In reality, all that happens is that you have a country full of disarmed innocents at the mercy of the criminals, completely dependent on law enforcement officers (which are in short supply) to protect them.<P>This new bill uses the same backwards logic. Force the population to abandon their older cars in favor of newer cars with improved technology. But a large portion of the newer vehicles are SUVs and trucks that get WORSE fuel economy than some of the vehicles they would be replacing.<P>DUH<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000018||fieroX||12-13-2001||08:18 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Blacktree:<BR><B><BR>That is, if they (the gov't) haven't taken your win mag away by then...<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Again, come and get the win mag.  They are going to fight the same battle.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by fieroX (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Boomtastic||12-19-2001||07:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick's Dad:<BR><B>Hi Guys,<P>I got this from SEMA last night:<P> URGENT FEDERAL SCRAPPAGE ALERT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I received my copy from SEMA as well, but did not post it anywhere after the last "episode". A few months back SEMA announced that our state (Mass) was proposing legislation that would ban aftermarket mufflers (*all* - not just the 'rice' style, but ALL). I posted it to a few lists that I was on and the flame war began! I received all sorts of hate mail, running the gamut of people wanting to stick a muffler somewhere "where the sun don't shine" to ones that just were pissed that they had to move their mouse from their AOL Instant Messenger to the Delete button in their email. In short, no one really wanted to hear about the topic. At that point I gave up posting SEMA related news. This is very saddening, as it ultimately affects us all one way or the other. People should be aware of what their legislatures are doing without our knowledge. A classic example of this is our seat belt law, which has been voted "in" by our legislatures 4 times, and "out" by the constituents 3 times. Everytime they vote the law in, we vote it out. OBVIOUSLY, we don't want the law, yet it keeps turning up like a bad penny. (Personally, I don't want a law to tell me I have to wear a seat belt. I wear it willingly, and don't believe the government should be put in the capacity to think for me. I'm a big boy now .. If one chooses not to wear his/her seat belt, that's their decision alone.) During the time that the law is in effect, motorists are stopped and fined for violations. Once the law is repealed, the ticketing stops, however the money is not returned. (Not even a Thank You card from the State House!) These people that bitched me out about the mufflers are the same ones that will cry when they can't find one to fit their vehicle 5 years down the road, or they are forced to pay the dealerships extreme amounts of cash for an OEM one. I say get involved with SEMA and find out how your rights as a motorist are being squeezed. Kudos for bringing the SEMA Action Alert into the light. I'll be standing over here with the fire extinguisher, just in case ....<P>------------------<BR>Boomtastic<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mirror_md_clr.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000020||FieroRacer||12-19-2001||07:37 PM||||Let's see their FWD crown vics and tow trucks try catching our cars in traffic.  THey'll run out of gas from their 15+ gallon tanks before our 10 gallon tanks run dry!!!  Quick, call the EPA!!  We have several gas guzzling unsafe vehicles piled up on a turn on a freeway!!  While just cruising away in our fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000021||DaRkLoRD||12-19-2001||09:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Patrick's Dad:<BR><B>Now the eco-geeks want to take all of your cars (Those of us who aren't in CA or OH) and put a new Chevy Metro, Honda Insight, or Saturn EV1 into your driveway at a slight discount.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I consider myself a bit of an "eco-geek", but I hate these new "economy" cars.. they're ugly, underpowered, overpriced piles of junk.. especially the echo.. their mileage is barely better than a duke... heck a vw beetle with a turbo diesel engine and a 5spd gets what, 60mpg? it has some fairly respectable power too, considering the efficiency..<P>I'll be quite ticked off if I can't one day build the 1934 sedan street rod I want.. or fix up a late 60s Mustang GT...<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
